[Term]
id: HP:0000556
name: Retinal dystrophy
alt_id: HP:0007736
alt_id: HP:0007910
alt_id: HP:0007974
alt_id: HP:0007982
alt_id: HP:0030635
def: "Retinal dystrophy is an abnormality of the retina associated with a hereditary process. Retinal dystrophies are defined by their predominantly monogenic inheritance and they are frequently associated with loss or dysfunction of photoreceptor cells as a primary or secondary event." [https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0986-4123]
synonym: "Breakdown of light-sensitive cells in back of eye" EXACT layperson [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6548-5200]
