[Term]
id: HP:0030828
name: Wheezing
def: "A high-pitched whistling sound associated with labored breathing." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199, PMID:26229557]
comment: Wheezes and rhonchi are continuous musical lung sounds. The American Thoracic Society (ATS) Committee on pulmonary nomenclature defines wheezes as high-pitched continuous sounds with a dominant frequency of 400 Hz or more, and rhonchi as low-pitched continuous musical sounds with a dominant frequency of about 200 Hz or less
synonym: "Wheezing" EXACT layperson []
