[Term]
id: MONDO:0003406
name: sleep-wake disorder
def: "Abnormal sleep-wake schedule or pattern associated with the circadian rhythm which affect the length, timing, and/or rigidity of the sleep-wake cycle relative to the day-night cycle. These can include dyssomnias such as circadian rhythm disorders, hypersomnia, and sleep apnea and parasomnias such as bruxism and rapid eye movement sleep disorder." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3458-4839, MESH:D012893]
