[Term]
id: MONDO:0006645
name: alcoholic polyneuropathy
def: "Any polyneuropathy where damage to the peripheral nervous system (including the peripheral elements of the autonomic nervous system) is associated with chronic ingestion of alcoholic beverages. The disorder may be caused by a direct effect of alcohol, an associated nutritional deficiency, or a combination of factors." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, MESH:D020269]
