[Term]
id: MONDO:0009665
name: biotinidase deficiency
def: "A late-onset form of multiple carboxylase deficiency, an inborn error of biotin metabolism that, if untreated, is characterized by seizures, breathing difficulties, hypotonia, skin rash, alopecia, hearing loss and delayed development." [Orphanet:79241]
synonym: "biotin deficiency" RELATED [GARD:0000894]
