[Term]
id: MONDO:0009696
name: juvenile myoclonic epilepsy
def: "The most common hereditary idiopathic generalized epilepsy syndrome and is characterized by myoclonic jerks of the upper limbs on awakening, generalized tonic-clonic seizures manifesting during adolescence and triggered by sleep deprivation, alcohol intake, and cognitive activities, and typical absence seizures (30% of cases)." [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:307]
