[Term]
id: MONDO:0009711
name: congenital fiber-type disproportion myopathy
def: "A rare genetic disorder caused by mutations in the TPM3, ACTA1, RYR1 or SEPN1 genes. It is inherited in an autosomal dominant or recessive pattern and rarely in an X-linked pattern. It manifests with myopathy throughout the body, particularly in the muscles of the shoulders, upper arms, hips, and thighs. Affected individuals may have contractures, lordosis, or scoliosis. In a minority of cases mild to severe breathing problems may occur." [NCIT:C120046, PMID:31578728]
synonym: "CFTDM" EXACT ABBREVIATION [Orphanet:2020]
synonym: "congenital fiber type disproportion" RELATED [GARD:0006161]
