[Term]
id: MONDO:0011577
name: myopathy, proximal, and ophthalmoplegia
def: "Any congenital myopathy in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in MYH2 gene. The disorder is either slowly progressive or nonprogressive, and affected individuals retain ambulation, although there is variable severity. It can show both autosomal dominant and autosomal recessive inheritance." [OMIM:605637]
synonym: "inclusion body myopathy 3, autosomal dominant" RELATED [OMIM:605637]
synonym: "myopathy with congenital joint contractures, ophthalmoplegia, and rimmed vacuoles" EXACT [OMIM:605637]
