[Term]
id: MONDO:0012992
name: pancreatic insufficiency-anemia-hyperostosis syndrome
def: "A rare syndromic mitochondrial disease in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the COX4I2 gene. It is characterized by exocrine pancreatic insufficiency, dyserythropoietic anemia, and calvarial hyperostosis." [Orphanet:199337]
