[Term]
id: MONDO:0013731
name: MEGF10-related myopathy
def: "A congenital myopathy caused by mutations in the multiple epidermal growth factor-like domains 10 (MEGF10) gene, which causes early-onset myopathy characterized by severe weakness, scoliosis, joint contractures, areflexia, respiratory distress, and dysphagia, and a milder phenotype of minicore myopathy." [PMID:22371254, PMID:27460346]
synonym: "congenital myopathy 10A, severe variant" EXACT [OMIM:614399]
synonym: "early-onset myopathy, areflexia, respiratory distress and dysphagia" RELATED [GARD:0012199]
