[Term]
id: MONDO:0017343
name: Epstein-Barr virus-associated lymphoproliferative disorder
def: "A range of lymphoproliferative diseases characterized by uncontrolled proliferation of B cells, T cells, or NK cells infected with Epstein-Barr virus. Depending on host immunity and viral factors, viral persistence in host cells can induce lymphoproliferation with a diverse clinical spectrum ranging from simple reactive hyperplasia to aggressive lymphoma/leukemia with unique clinical and pathological presentations." [PMID:38882456]
comment: the classification of diseases such as HL and BL under this class is not consistent with MONDO design patterns, since not all instances of these diseases are caused by EBV
synonym: "EBV-associated lymphoproliferative disorder" EXACT [Orphanet:289644]
synonym: "Epstein-Barr virus-associated malignant lymphoproliferative disorder" NARROW []
