[Term]
id: MONDO:0019195
name: hereditary inclusion body myopathy-joint contractures-ophthalmoplegia syndrome
def: "A rare genetic neuromuscular disease characterized by early onset of proximal or generalized muscle weakness, external ophthalmoplegia with or without ptosis, and joint contractures. Hypotonia, neonatal respiratory distress necessitating ventilation, and severe dysphagia have also been reported. The disease is of variable severity and non- or slowly progressive. Patients typically remain ambulatory. Muscle biopsy may show predominance of type 1 fibers, marked variability in fiber size, increased internal nuclei, and proliferation of perimysial and endomysial connective tissue." [Orphanet:79091]
synonym: "Hereditary inclusion body myopathy - joint contractures - ophthalmoplegia" RELATED [GARD:0009494]
synonym: "Hereditary inclusion body myopathy type 3" RELATED [GARD:0009494]
synonym: "hereditary inclusion body myopathy type 3" EXACT [Orphanet:79091]
synonym: "HIBM3" EXACT ABBREVIATION [GARD:0009494, Orphanet:79091]
synonym: "IBM3" EXACT ABBREVIATION [GARD:0009494, Orphanet:79091]
