[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1203
name: Sodium voltage-gated channel alpha subunits
is_a: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/178 ! Voltage-gated ion channels
is_a: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/179 ! Sodium channels
property_value: terms:description "Sodium channels are voltage-gated sodium-selective ion channels present in the membrane of most excitable cells. Sodium channels comprise of one pore-forming α subunit, which may be associated with either one or two beta subunits. Alpha-subunits consist of four homologous domains (I–IV), each containing six transmembrane segments (S1–S6) and a pore-forming loop. The positively charged fourth transmembrane segment (S4) acts as a voltage sensor and is involved in channel gating." xsd:string

