is_a: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/3349 ! Methyltransferase families grouped by structure

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/130
name: Aminoacyl tRNA synthetases
synonym: "aaRS" RELATED []
is_a: SO:0005855 ! gene group
property_value: terms:description "An aminoacyl tRNA synthetase ( aaRS ) is an enzyme that catalyzes the esterification of a specific amino acid or its precursor to one of all its compatible cognate tRNAs to form an aminoacyl-tRNA. In other words, aminoacyl tRNA synthetase simply attaches the appropriate, or 'cognate,' amino acid onto the corresponding tRNA. This is sometimes called 'charging' or 'loading' the tRNA with the amino acid. Once the tRNA is charged, a ribosome can transfer the amino acid from the tRNA onto a growing peptide, according to the genetic code." xsd:string

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/131
name: Aminoacyl tRNA synthetases, Class I
is_a: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/130 ! Aminoacyl tRNA synthetases

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1318
name: Non-canonical poly(A) polymerases
synonym: "TUTases" RELATED []
is_a: SO:0005855 ! gene group
property_value: terms:description "Polyadenylation of mitochondrial RNAs in higher eukaryotic organisms have diverse effects on their function and metabolism. Polyadenylation completes the UAA stop codon of a majority of mitochondrial mRNAs in mammals, regulates the translation of the mRNAs, and has diverse effects on their stability.    The addition of a poly(A) tail is catalyzed by poly(A) polymerases (PAPs). Nuclear PAPs that are involved in the 3′-end processing of pre-mRNAs have been studied extensively over the years. More recently, a collection of non-canonical PAPs (ncPAPs) has been identified, which are involved in polyadenylation in other organelles (as well as in the nucleus). Some of these ncPAPs have relaxed base selectivity and can also synthesize oligo- or poly-uridylate tails, and hence are also known as poly(U) polymerases (PUPs) or terminal uridylate transferases (TUTs or TUTases)." xsd:string

[Term]
