property_value: terms:description "This family consists of the G protein alpha subunit group I (inhibitory), which includes G alpha-I, G alpha-O, G alpha-T and G alpha-Z. G alpha-I proteins were originally identified by their receptor-mediated inhibition of the cAMP-generating enzyme adenylyl cyclase." xsd:string

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1430
name: G protein subunits beta
synonym: "G(I)/G(S)/G(T) subunits beta" RELATED []
synonym: "GNB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "guanine nucleotide-binding protein G(I)/G(S)/G(T) subunits beta" RELATED []
is_a: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1431 ! Heterotrimeric G proteins
property_value: terms:description "Guanine nucleotide binding proteins (G proteins) are membrane-associated, heterotrimeric proteins composed of three subunits: alpha, beta and gamma. This entry consists of the G protein beta subunit, which assumes a barrel-shaped beta-propeller structure containing WD-40 repeats preceded by an N-terminal alpha helix. The beta subunit forms a stable dimer with the gamma subunit. The alpha subunit only contacts the beta subunit in the dimer, lying on the opposite face from the gamma subunit." xsd:string

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/1431
name: Heterotrimeric G proteins
synonym: "G-proteins" RELATED []
synonym: "Guanosine nucleotide-binding proteins" RELATED []
synonym: "Large G proteins" RELATED []
is_a: SO:0005855 ! gene group
property_value: terms:description "'G protein' usually refers to the membrane-associated heterotrimeric G proteins, sometimes referred to as the 'large' G proteins (as opposed to the subclass of smaller, monomeric small GTPases). These proteins are activated by G protein-coupled receptors and are made up of alpha, beta and gamma subunits, the latter two referred to as the beta-gamma complex" xsd:string

