name: Short chain dehydrogenase/reductase superfamily
synonym: "SDR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "SDR family" RELATED []
is_a: SO:0005855 ! gene group
property_value: terms:description "The short-chain dehydrogenases/reductases family (SDR) is a very large family of enzymes, most of which are known to be NAD- or NADP-dependent oxidoreductases." xsd:string

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/746
name: Solute carrier family 56, sideroflexins
synonym: "Sideroflexin family" RELATED []
synonym: "Sideroflexins" RELATED []
synonym: "SLC56 Sideroflexins" RELATED []
synonym: "SLC56, SFXN" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Solute carrier family 56" RELATED []
is_a: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/752 ! Solute carrier families

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/752
name: Solute carrier families
synonym: "SLC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
is_a: SO:0005855 ! gene group
property_value: terms:description "The solute carrier (SLC) group of membrane transport proteins include over 400 members organized into 66 families. Most members of the SLC group are located in the cell membrane." xsd:string

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/757
name: SRY-box transcription factors
synonym: "Sex determining region Y boxes" RELATED []
synonym: "SOX" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Sox family" RELATED []
synonym: "Sry-related HMG boxes" RELATED []
is_a: SO:0005855 ! gene group
property_value: terms:description "SOX genes encode a family of transcription factors that bind to the minor groove in DNA, and belong to a super-family of genes characterized by a homologous sequence called the HMG-box (for high mobility group ). This HMG box is a DNA binding domain that is highly conserved throughout eukaryotic species. Homologues have been identified in insects, nematodes, amphibians, reptiles, birds and a range of mammals. However, HMG boxes can be very diverse in nature, with only a few amino acids being conserved between species.  Sox genes are defined as containing the HMG box of a gene involved in sex determination called SRY, which resides on the Y-chromosome (Sox stands for Sry-related HMG box). There are 20 SOX genes present in humans and mice, and 8 present in Drosophila. Almost all Sox genes show at least 50% amino acid similarity with the HMG box in Sry. The family is divided into subgroups according to homology within the HMG domain and other structural motifs, as well as according to functional assays.   " xsd:string

[Term]
id: https://www.genenames.org/data/genegroup/#!/group/760
name: Sterile alpha motif domain containing
synonym: "SAM domain containing" RELATED []
synonym: "SAMD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
is_a: SO:0005855 ! gene group

